# Cookie & tracking check: http://localhost:8721/ (site mode, target country: CZ)

**Summary:** I crawled the site three times: with no interaction, after rejecting, and after accepting. On every page load, before the visitor makes any choice, the site sets Google Analytics and Meta Pixel cookies, writes a Hotjar key to localStorage, and sends requests to Meta and Google. Choosing in the banner changes nothing: the page source shows these scripts run with no consent check at all. The banner has no "reject all" on its first layer, its marketing and statistics boxes are already ticked, its text is English only on a Czech site, there is no way to withdraw consent later, and there is no privacy policy link. The page title ("Špatný e-shop", meaning "bad e-shop") and the HTML comments suggest this is a deliberately broken test page. All findings still hold for what is actually served.

**Tested:** 2026-11-08, crawler 0.1.0 (Playwright/Chromium), locale `cs-CZ`, states: no interaction, reject (Settings → Save settings), accept (Accept all). Pages: `/` and `/page2.html`. I also read the served HTML with `curl` to confirm the cause.
**Limits:** Localhost over HTTP, so the cookie security attributes (L21) don't tell us much. I didn't check location, A/B variants or bot detection, though they are unlikely to matter for a static local page. The crawler's "reject" path clicked Save without unticking the pre-ticked boxes. That doesn't change the result, because the page code ignores the boxes entirely (see L4). The crawl sent real requests with test IDs to `facebook.com` and `google-analytics.com`.

## Presumptive violations
| ID | Finding | Evidence | Countries where it matters most | Suggested fix |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| L1 | Tracking cookies set before any choice | `_ga` (GA, 400 d), `_ga_TEST123` (GA, 400 d), `_fbp` (Meta Pixel, 90 d), first-party, `localhost`. Written by the inline `<script>` in `<head>` (`document.cookie = "_ga=…"`, `"_fbp=…"`) and by gtag.js | CZ (ÚOOÚ type "no consent"; § 89(3) Act 127/2005 Sb.) | Load trackers only after an opt-in for the matching purpose (CMP-gated loading or `type="text/plain"` with a category attribute) |
| L2 | Hotjar identifier in localStorage before any choice | `localStorage._hjSessionUser_123` from the inline script (`localStorage.setItem('_hjSessionUser_123', …)`) | CZ | Write it only after statistics consent, or remove it |
| L3 | Tracker requests before any choice | `https://www.facebook.com/tr?id=123&ev=PageView`; `https://region1.google-analytics.com/g/collect?v=2&tid=G-TEST123…`; `https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-TEST123` | CZ | Same as L1 |
| L4 | Refusing has no effect: cookies, storage and the Meta Pixel are still there after "reject" and fire again on `/page2.html` | The cookies and storage key above stay after the choice. `facebook.com/tr` was requested on `/` and `/page2.html` after the choice. In the source, the Save button only writes `consent=custom` and closes the banner. No script reads the `consent` cookie or the `#mkt`/`#stat` boxes | CZ (ÚOOÚ type "banner ignoring choices") | Make every tracker conditional on the stored choice. Delete `_ga*`, `_fbp` and `_hj*` when the visitor refuses or withdraws |
| L6 | No "reject all" on the first layer. Refusing takes 2 clicks (Settings → Save), accepting takes 1 | Visible controls on the first layer are only "Accept all" and "Settings" | CZ: ÚOOÚ expects reject on the same layer as accept | Add an "Odmítnout vše" (Reject all) button next to "Přijmout vše" (Accept all) |
| L8 | Marketing and statistics are pre-ticked | `<input type="checkbox" id="mkt" checked>`, `<input … id="stat" checked>` | All (Planet49 C-673/17) | Leave all non-essential boxes unticked by default |
| L14 | No way to change or withdraw consent | No footer link or floating icon found. Also, the banner shows again on every page because the choice is never read back | CZ (ÚOOÚ type "impossible withdrawal"; GDPR art. 7(3)) | Add a "Nastavení cookies" (Cookie settings) footer link that reopens the settings, and remember the choice |
| L22 | Banner is English only on a Czech-language site | `<html lang="cs">`, Czech content ("Vítejte", "Další stránka"); banner: "We use cookies to improve your experience. Accept all · Settings" | **CZ**: ÚOOÚ lists "English-only information" as one of its six violation types, so I raised this from warning to presumptive violation for CZ | Translate the banner, settings and policy into Czech |

## Warnings
| ID | Finding | Evidence | Suggested fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| L7 | Accept and reject are not visually equal | Accept: green `#27ae60` button, 174×51 px, 20 px bold white text. Settings: 55×16 px, 12 px grey `#555` underlined text on `#222`, contrast about 2.1:1 | Use the same size, style and contrast for both buttons |
| L12 | Google tag with no Consent Mode default | `gtag('config','G-TEST123')` runs with no prior `gtag('consent','default',…)`. The dataLayer had no default call (Google contract, not EU law) | Before `config`, set `ad_storage`, `analytics_storage`, `ad_user_data` and `ad_personalization` to `denied` |
| L19 | Canvas fingerprinting API called before any choice | `canvas.toDataURL` from the inline script on `/` and `/page2.html` (commented "Fingerprinting before consent") | Remove it, or run it only after consent if it is not strictly necessary |
| L16 | No cookie or privacy policy found | No policy link on either page | Publish a Czech cookie policy listing each cookie, its purpose, lifetime, third party and any transfers, and link it from the banner and footer |
| L21 | No `Secure`/`HttpOnly` flags | All cookies have `secure:false, httpOnly:false`. `PHPSESSID` is set from JS, so it can't be HttpOnly | In production, set the session cookie server-side with `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` |

## Needs human review
| Item | Why automation stops here | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `shop_ab_test` | An A/B-test cookie is usually not strictly necessary. Only you know what it is used for | `variant-b`, 30 d, first-party, set before any choice |
| `consent` | A consent-state cookie is usually necessary, but this one has no expiry and is never read | Session cookie, value `all` or `custom` |
| `PHPSESSID` | Likely necessary, but it is set by client JS with a fixed value (`abc123`), which is unusual | Session cookie, first-party |
| L24 transfers | Meta and Google are US recipients. The Data Privacy Framework status and any transfer assessment need a human | Requests to `facebook.com` and `google-analytics.com` |
| L17 proof of consent | No consent log endpoint was seen | — |

## Observed facts
- **Before any choice:** cookies `_ga`, `_ga_TEST123`, `_fbp`, `PHPSESSID`, `shop_ab_test`; localStorage `_hjSessionUser_123`; requests to gtag.js, `facebook.com/tr` and GA4 `/g/collect`; `canvas.toDataURL` called.
- **After "reject":** the same as before, plus `consent=custom`. The Pixel and gtag.js fire again on reload and on `/page2.html`. The banner shows again on every page.
- **After "accept all":** Meta Pixel, Google Analytics and Hotjar. The result is identical to the other two states, so there is no gating at all.
- **Banner:** fixed bottom bar, English text, first-layer controls "Accept all" and "Settings". The second layer has Necessary (locked), Marketing ☑ and Statistics ☑, plus "Save settings".
- **Withdrawal control:** none. **Policy links:** none.

